{"id":"stmt:ono2022@handbook-epub/l0080-04","source":"source:ono2022","asset":"asset:ono2022@handbook-epub","locator":{"leaf":80,"printed":"12.8","section":null,"example":null},"anchor":{"exact":"Another famous example is irankarapte,[175] a polite greeting in the Ainu language and the most famous of all Ainu greetings. It is usually given by a man who is happy to see someone again, while performing the traditional manner of showing respect (onkami or onkamuy). In other words, it is not a casual greeting to friends and acquaintances in everyday life.","match":1,"method":"exact","leaf":80},"statement":{"en":"The polite greeting irankarapte is traditionally given by a man happy to see someone again while performing the ritual gesture of respect (onkami or onkamuy), rather than used as a casual everyday greeting.","ja":"丁寧な挨拶である irankarapte は、伝統的には再会を喜ぶ男性によって敬意を示す伝統的作法（オンカミまたはオンカムイ）を行いながら交わされるものであり、日常的な気軽な挨拶ではない。"},"type":"form-function","stance":"asserts","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["traditional usage"]},"hedge":null,"reported":null,"forms":["irankarapte","onkami","onkamuy"],"topics":["topic:discourse/gendered-register-speech","topic:register/honorific-ritual-and-taboo-registers","topic:discourse/gendered-register-speech--ritual-speech"],"extracted_by":"act:extract/ono2022/2026-09-10T13-38-52-536Z","verification":{"anchor":"pass","image":"not-applicable","entailment":{"verdict":"yes","quote":"It is usually given by a man who is happy to see someone again, while performing the traditional manner of showing respect (onkami or onkamuy). In other words, it is not a casual greeting to friends and acquaintances in everyday life.","note":null,"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"verify-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"},"human":null},"status":"checked","routing":{"section":"topic:discourse/gendered-register-speech--ritual-speech","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash","prompt_version":"route-v1.0","date":"2026-09-10"}}
